win on p9web (github.com/cptaffe/plan9web): Plan 9's win, as this tree has it (9legacy's), on
plan9port's libthread and lib9p, which p9web's build compiles it with.

Changes for p9web (this branch's commit):
	main.c	threadexec (plan9port's libthread) in place of procexec; /mnt/acme in place of
		/mnt/wsys; no Scroll and Noscroll, and no scroll ctl message (plan9port's Acme
		scrolls by itself, and refuses them: its commit ba31ab30); ^C (0x03) is an
		interrupt too, as in plan9port's win, since that Acme erases with Delete; the
		typed interrupt is taken out of the body, as there
	win.c	/mnt/acme in place of /mnt/wsys; no noscroll ctl message

win serves cons and consctl (lib9p) and mounts them before /dev in its namespace; rc reads and
writes them. A note to rc's note group is an interrupt (Del, or ^C).
